NO-PYOCD-TARGET-FOR-ADUCM3029. `python -m pyocd list --targets` lists 1672
targets and not one of them matches "aducm", "adi" or "analog", so there is
no name to put here and none to `pyocd pack install` either. The
EVAL-ADICUP3029 carries a DAPLink that programs a .hex by drag and drop,
which is how rigs/fw_aducm_aes/ flashes it. tools/capture.py reads this
whole file as the target name, so it will hand this text to pyocd and pyocd
will refuse it. That is the intended loud failure: this port is untested on
silicon and nothing should flash from it silently.
